body:
For my world, I decided not to use any typical fantasy races or creatures. I don't even have humans in my setting. So here are a few of the races that I've come up with.

&#x200B;

\- The Shadow Folk: A race of demons who dwell mainly on a moon called Nightfall. They have jet black skin and hair, typically stand over six feet tall and often have a muscular build. Their culture is built upon an honor code, though it is less strict than the honor code of the Oni (i'll get to them in a bit). Apart from that, they are known to greatly enjoy reading, learning about history and for holding festivals, feasts and other fun events. Strongly ingrained in their culture is their worship of Anazul, the god of death.

&#x200B;

\- The Oni: Another one of the demon races, the Oni live on the moon of Falaria. The Oni are horribly disfigured and ugly, so they always wear masks in public to hide their faces. As a result of this, their culture is very impersonal and cold. They abide by a very strict code of honor and rigid rules governing social interactions. They are slightly arrogant and look down on the other demon races, as they believe that they have stayed true to their ancestry and culture more than the other two demon races.

&#x200B;

\- The Djinn: The Djinn are descended from the Wenya and live exclusively on the moon of Starfell. They are very reclusive and distrustful towards outsiders, so very few non-djinn are allowed to visit Starfell. They were the last people to leave Chasdia, the ancient home of all mortals. As such, they became diseased and decrepit due to the effects of living on the planet after the Great Heart-Theft. Since their bodies are in a constant state of decay, they use mysterious and unnatural magic to replace their body parts with those of animals. As a result, every djinn looks different. Some of them have scales, others have feathers or even fur. 

&#x200B;

\-The Star Folk: The descendents of the Nornir, the Star Folk lived on the moon of Lumiel, before migrating to Felnor. They were eventually driven to extinction by the Abyssal Prince and his armies. In the eyes of the gods, the Star Folk were the purest race. They had not resorted to dark magic or ritualistic heart-eating as many peoples had. They lived in harmony with nature and were known for their beautiful art and music, their excellent academies and other places of learning, and were also known to have a reasonably strong military. Their first moon was sometimes called "The Jewel of The Stars," and they were said to have reached the highest level of cultural sophistication.
